-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",39,{
[1217]="70009815\n1\tCollect faded scroll-fragments (quantity: see journal)\030Collect worn scroll-fragments (quantity: see journal)\tBrigands and robbers can be found in many places around Lake Evendim. Brigands and tomb-robbers in Evendim most likely hold the remaining fragments of the scroll you found.\n2\tTalk to Culang\030Collect Old Scroll-fragment\030Collect Faded Scroll-fragment\030Collect Worn Scroll-fragment\tTinnudir, an island west of Emyn Uial, may have a lore-master who can help you reassemble the scroll. You found all the scroll-fragments; now all you have to do is put them together.\n3\tRecover the treasure from the old trove\tThe old trove is hidden beneath a stone marker, north-east of Tinnudír in the ruins of Barad Rath. Culang helped to reconstruct the old scroll and told you the good news: not only does it give directions to an old treasure, but the treasure is one that can be honourably recovered, since there is no record of the original owners.\n4\tTalk to Culang\030Collect Restored Scroll\030Collect Battle-chronicles\tCulang can be found back at Tinnudir. You found no great treasure; it appears that the old trove had been looted long ago. But you did recover an old book: a chronicle of the Battle of Fornost. Perhaps Culang would find it of interest, along with the scroll he restored for you.\n",
[1218]="7002CDA5\n1\tTalk to Doron\tDoron has brought you to the ruins of Ost Celebrant in search of the Easterling invader. Doron believes that the Easterling lurks somewhere in the tunnels below Ost Celebrant.\n2\tTalk to Doron\tDoron can be summoned to your side by using your horn.\n",
[1219]="7002D3A1\n1\tFind Túbi Thickfist at the top of the Stair\tTúbi Thickfist is atop the great stairway of Durin's Threshold. You should climb the stairs and find Túbi Thickfist.\n",
[1220]="700345E3\n1\tFind out what watches you from the trees\tYou sense that unfriendly eyes watch you from nearby, hidden from your sight....\n2\tDrive off sneaking enemies in the wood (total: 3)\tSome stealthed creature watches you from the trees surrounding Dunfast in the Whitshaws. You should find and drive off the unfriendly presence in the woods.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have driven away the spying goblins encircling Dunfast, waiting to raise the alarm if the people dared to return.\n",
[1221]="70071DFB\n1\tInvestigate the Blade-horn for a suspicious man\tInvestigate the Blade-horn to find the culprit in a series of recent disappearances.\n2\tDefeat the ordinary-looking man\tDefeat this ordinary-looking man in the Blade-horn.\n3\tDefeat the ordinary-looking man again\tPursue and defeat the ordinary-looking man in the Blade-horn.\n4\tPursue and defeat the ordinary-looking man\tPursue and defeat the ordinary-looking man deeper in the Blade-horn.\n",
[1222]="70015E48\n1\tBring the necklace to Ladenthir in Echad Eregion\tLadenthir is in Echad Eregion, south of High Hollin. You should bring the necklace to Ladenthir for further inspection.\n",
[1223]="70020BB5\n1\tComplete A Healing Hand\030Complete Warmth for the Winter\030Complete Feathers for Friendship\tSaeradan, Andreg, and Amlan are at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith. Saeradan has asked you to aid the Grey Company in their many tasks. He told you that he had a task for you, and that Amlan and Andreg might as well.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith. You should speak with Saeradan regarding his plans for the items you collected.\n3\tDeliver the peace offering to the Algraig goatherds at Gavar Cadlus\tThe Algraig goatherds are at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan, along the foothills of the Misty Mountains. Saeradan asked you to deliver the herbs, pelts, and feathers you collected to the Algraig goatherds as a peace offering.\n",
[1224]="70020BB2\n1\tBring the pelts, feathers, and herbs to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus\tGrufudh is at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan. Saeradan has asked you to deliver more pelts, feathers, and herbs to Grufudh the goatherd.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith, south-west of Gavar Cadlus. Grufudh told you to return to Saeradan with the thanks of his people and assurance that supplies will be sent.\n",
[1225]="70066274\n1\tLook for Orthor at Amon Lontir\tCenedel has asked you to check Amon Lontir and see whether Orthor is there. Amon Lontir is located just outside of Ost Lontir.\n2\tTalk to Orthor\tYou have found Orthor at Amon Lontir. You should talk to him.\n3\tTalk to Mildir at Ost Lontir\tOrthor has asked you to deliver an apology note to Mildir. Mildir can be found in Ost Lontir.\n",
[1226]="70066EE7\n1\tDefeat sickle-flies and angry gnats for Mousy Othwen (total: 8)\tSickle-flies and angry gnats are a constant irritation for Mousy Othwen, a somewhat eccentric resident of Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to Mousy Othwen in southern Tadrent, in King's Gondor\tMousy Othwen is in southern Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n",
[1227]="7002F59E\n1\tReclaim Rohirrim weapons from the Orcs (total: 4)\030Reclaim Rohirrim armour-pieces from the Orcs (total: 4)\tOrcs can be found scavenging in the fields around Elthengels. Baldthorne has asked you to recover any Rohirrim weapons or armour-pieces from the Orcs, to help him supply the guards and garrison.\n2\tReturn the weapons and armour-pieces to Baldthorne\tBaldthorne is awaiting the reclaimed weapons and armour at his smith in Elthengels. You have reclaimed the weapons and armour pieces, once taken by the Orcs from Rohirrim.\n",
[1228]="70028FBE\n1\tCraft the staves you collect into spears (total: 14)\tBowstaves are scattered about the worksite. Wunne has asked you to help craft spears. You should collect many bowstaves. Once you collect them, they can be used from your inventory to craft spears.\n2\tBring the spears you crafted to Wunne\tWunne can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev. You should bring the spears you made to Wunne so that she can deliver them to Flint Ironheart.\n",
[1229]="70016745\n1\tBury the fallen dwarves (total: 4)\tYou found dwarf-corpses in the place called Mazam-dûm, on the eastern side of the lake in the Foundations of Stone. Nökkvi has asked you to bury the dwarf-corpses you found.\n2\tTalk to Nökkvi at the Shadowed Refuge\tNökkvi is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone. You should return to Nökkvi to tell him of the burials you performed.\n",
[1230]="70036FDC\n1\tDefeat bears (total: 9)\030Collect bear-hides (total: 6)\tBears are hunting in the Roaring Hills to the south of the road where Oter and Stithwulf are camped. Stithwulf asked you to hunt the bears and bring back any unblemished hides that you are able to collect.\n2\tPlace the bear-hides on the waggon\tStithwulf and Oter's camp lies to the north of the Roaring Hills. Stithwulf asked you to bring any intact hides back to his camp to help bolster supplies for the long road.\n3\tReturn to Stithwulf\tStithwulf is at his camp in the Stonedeans, north of the Roaring Hills. Stithwulf would like to thank you for ensuring the safety of their camp and returning with hides.\n",
[1231]="70034FAF\n1\tTell Cyneberg that Gárwig wishes her to search Byre Tor\tCyneberg has come to Lornsettle, the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n2\tTell Gárwig of Cyneberg's denial\tGárwig is in Lornsettle, the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You should speak with Gárwig.\n3\tTry to convince Cyneberg to return to Gárwig, and accept her grief\tCyneberg ran off to ready herself for a journey to the High Knolls to search for Thrymm. You should search for Cyneberg in Forlaw.\n4\tTell Gárwig that Cyneberg will not obey\tGárwig is in Lornsettle, the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You should return to Gárwig.\n",
[1232]="7002F930\n1\tConvince Giselmon to donate food to the refugees\tGiselmon can be found at her estate in the western section of Cliving. Isenyd has asked you to convince Giselmon that hosting a banquet in times of great turmoil would be distasteful and cause her to lose popularity.\n2\tTalk to the butcher of Cliving\030Talk to the cheese-maker of Cliving\030Talk to the baker of Cliving\tThe vendors can be found at their individual stands in the marketplace, west of the central fountain in Cliving. Giselmon has asked you to speak with the food-vendors in Cliving, in order to divert a large portion of her purchases to help those in need.\n3\tTalk to Giselmon in Cliving\tGiselmon can be found at her estate in the western section of Cliving. You may inform Giselmon that the vendors were pleased to help her send portions of her orders to be donated to the needy.\n",
[1233]="7002EEF6\n1\tTalk to Frána\t\n2\tTalk to Frána\tFrána is hiding near the Mead Hall of Thornhope. You should escort Frána to safety.\n3\tTalk to Frána at Béortnoth's camp\tFrána is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope. You should speak with Frána when you return to Béortnoth's camp.\n",
[1234]="70061222\n1\tFish for the tiny waterlogged boot\tFish for the lost boot in the nearby pond.\n2\tReturn the boot to Maggo Bunce\tMaggo Bunce is near the pond south-east of Nobottle. Deliver the boot to Maggo Bunce.\n",
[1235]="7000D605\n1\tTalk to Raith\tRaith is at Crannog's ruling-seat, west of the centre island of Aughaire. Nekhtan has told you that he is satisfied: you have proven to be worthy of taking his place in Clúcath against the Trév Duvárdain.\n",
[1236]="7002C5F4\n1\tExamine debris by the crumbling corner in Ost Celebrant\030Examine debris by the grassy place overlooking the fast-flowing river\030Examine debris by the stone bridge\tThe crumbling corner, the grassy river-overlook, and the stone bridge can be found in Parth Celebrant. Cerdic went searching some more locations of the ancient battlefield, and experienced strange sensations at some of them. He has marked them on your map and wants you to see what is happening at these sites.\n2\tTalk to Cerdic\tCerdic is at the watch-post on the road in Parth Celebrant. You have investigated the sites Cerdic told you about, and should now return to him.\n",
[1237]="700430AE\n1\tArvellon's folk can be found throughout Glaniath in Upper Lebennin. Arvellon has asked you to convince his people to seek refuge in Tumladen.\t\n2\tTalk to Arvellon\tArvellon can be found at the southern entrance to Glaniath in Upper Lebennin. You have urged the folk to seek shelter in Tumladen and should now return to Arvellon.\n",
[1238]="7002E79E\n1\tTalk to Simbi in the Twenty-first Hall\tSimbi is in the Twenty-first Hall, to the north-east of the Water-works. Kaldi wishes you to bring word of the Watcher's return to the expedition.\n",
[1239]="70047A87\n1\tEnter the maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk\tThe maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk are located in the Slag-hills. You should collect bones within the caverns.\n2\tCollect bones (total: 12)\tThe maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk are located in the Slag-hills. You should collect bones within the caverns.\n3\tBuild bone idols (total: 3)\tThe maggot-hole caverns of Skoironk are located in the Slag-hills. You should build idols with the bones to confuse the Orcs.\n4\tCompleted\tConfused many Orcs in Skoironk.\n",
[1240]="70047BE8\n1\tTalk to Artamir at Tham Durlan\tArtamir can be found at Tham Durlan in south-western Dagorlad. You have had a strange encounter with a shade of Gondor and should now tell Artamir about what you have seen and heard.\n2\tTalk to the accursed warrior at Tham Durlan\tThe accursed warrior has appeared at Tham Durlan in Dagorlad. You have told Artamir of the strange connexion between him and the accursed warrior, and now the shade has appeared at his side. You should try to uncover the shade's purpose in coming to Tham Durlan.\n3\tTalk to Artamir\tArtamir can be found at Tham Durlan in Dagorlad. The accursed warrior has not spoken to you since his arrival, but offered Artamir a grim warning. You should talk with Artamir about what is to be done.\n",
[1241]="7002FCCA\n1\tDefeat Half-orcs in the fields of Garsfeld (total: 8)\tHalf-orcs can be found on the crofts surrounding Garsfeld.\n2\tTalk to Gísil\tGísil can be found inside the mead-hall of Garsfeld.\n",
[1242]="7006A9E8\n1\tFind the camp Nashôn described\tTravel to the western areas of Ilmabiri and locate the camp of homeless children.\n2\tDefeat goblins (total: 6)\tYou have located the camp Nashôn described, but he was mistaken. This is not a camp for children.\n3\tInvestigate the goblin camp\tYou have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. You should look around the camp for clues explaining why they are here.\n4\tRead the note\tYou have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. While investigating the camp, you have spotted a note.\n5\tTalk to Nashôn\tYou have discovered a camp of goblins inside Ilmabiri. While investigating the camp, you have spotted a note indicating that they have recently come from Súlstrok to attempt to rescue their leader, Shakfut Slit-throat, from the fighting pits of the arena.\n",
[1243]="700572FC\n1\tAttend the 'Secret Meeting'\tGrímyr would like to speak with you privately. You should speak with him to attend the 'Secret Meeting'.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin\tYou have been accused of murder! You should talk to King Thorin.\n",
[1244]="7002C2B0\n1\tRelease Magla from his bonds\tMagla remains captured in the southern Wailing Hills. Magla has asked you to release him from his bonds, so that he may escape the Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Magla at the Cuthstan-camp\tMagla has fled back to the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan. Magla is awaiting your return at camp. He has something to discuss with you.\n",
[1245]="70066875\n1\tTalk to Malthellam\tTBD\n2\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tTBD\n",
[1246]="7004EA89\n1\tTalk to Vaskorn\tThrekmóth asked you to check on Vaskorn's condition.\n2\tTalk to Threkmóth\tThrekmóth can be found in Skoghús, in the south of Thornholt. Vaskorn is not feeling well. You should return to Threkmóth and update him.\n3\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in the north of the Thornholt woods. With Vaskorn's condition not improving, Radagast should be notified in case there is something he can do for the Beorning.\n4\tTalk to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld\tYou should return to Stráhek the Stout in Skarháld and tell him what took place in the woods.\n",
[1247]="7004E1E1\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. King Thorin III has received an urgent summons from Dís, the Keeper of Ravenhill, and has asked you to accompany him to Ravenhill. You should talk to King Thorin III when you are prepared.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You travelled to Ravenhill and witnessed the return of the raven-chief, Arcah. King Thorin pledged to honour the old ways of friendship between Durin's Folk and the ravens of the North, and in return, Arcah sent her ravens to spy upon the plots of Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind.\n",
[1248]="70030C88\n1\tTalk to Rook\tRook is atop his avanc to the west of Snowbourn in the Sutcrofts.\n2\tSearch Rook's avanc\tRook may have left some of his trappings on his avanc.\n",
})
